  },
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 1. 🟢 Gradient of a Linear Function\nCompute the gradient $\\nabla_\\mathbf{x} f$ where $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a}^T \\mathbf{x}$ for $\\mathbf{a} = [3, -1, 2]^T$. Verify numerically."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 2. 🟢 Gradient of Quadratic Form\nCompute $\\nabla_\\mathbf{x}(\\mathbf{x}^T A \\mathbf{x})$ for a symmetric matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\end{bmatrix}$ and verify that $\\nabla_\\mathbf{x} f = 2A\\mathbf{x}$."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 3. 🟢 Jacobian Computation\nCompute the Jacobian of $\\mathbf{f}(x_1, x_2) = \\begin{bmatrix} x_1^2 x_2 \\\\ 5x_1 + \\sin(x_2) \\end{bmatrix}$ symbolically using SymPy."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 4. 🔵 Chain Rule with Jacobians\nLet $\\mathbf{u} = A\\mathbf{x}$ and $f(\\mathbf{u}) = \\|\\mathbf{u}\\|^2$. Use the matrix chain rule to derive $\\nabla_\\mathbf{x} f = 2A^T A \\mathbf{x}$. Verify numerically."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 5. 🔵 Softmax Jacobian\nDerive and implement the Jacobian of the softmax function $\\sigma(\\mathbf{z})_i = \\frac{e^{z_i}}{\\sum_j e^{z_j}}$. Show that $\\frac{\\partial \\sigma_i}{\\partial z_j} = \\sigma_i(\\delta_{ij} - \\sigma_j)$."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 6. 🔵 Numerical vs Analytical Gradient Check\nImplement a function that compares the analytical gradient of $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\|A\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b}\\|^2$ against a finite-difference approximation."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 7. 🔵 Derivative of Matrix Inverse\nShow that $\\frac{d}{dt} A(t)^{-1} = -A(t)^{-1} \\frac{dA}{dt} A(t)^{-1}$ using the identity $A A^{-1} = I$ and the product rule."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your proof/verification here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 8. 🔵 Implement Forward-Mode AD for Multi-Variable Functions\nExtend the DualNumber class from the concepts notebook to support `__sub__`, `__truediv__`, and a `sin()` function. Use it to compute $\\nabla f$ for $f(x, y) = \\sin(x) / y + x^2$."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 9. 🔴 Backpropagation Through a 2-Layer MLP\nManually derive the gradient of the cross-entropy loss with respect to all weights $W_1, W_2$ and biases $b_1, b_2$ for a 2-layer MLP with ReLU activation: $\\hat{y} = \\text{softmax}(W_2 \\cdot \\text{ReLU}(W_1 \\mathbf{x} + b_1) + b_2)$."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your derivation and code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 10. 🔴 Build a Minimal Autograd Engine\nExtend the `Value` class from the concepts notebook to support `__sub__`, `__truediv__`, `__neg__`, `relu()`, and `tanh()`. Verify by training a tiny network on XOR."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 11. 🔴 Gradient of Log-Determinant\nDerive and verify numerically that $\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial X} \\log \\det(X) = X^{-T}$ for a positive definite matrix $X$."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 12. 🔴 JVP vs VJP Efficiency\nFor a function $f: \\mathbb{R}^{100} \\to \\mathbb{R}$, time the cost of computing the full gradient using (a) 100 JVPs (forward-mode) vs (b) 1 VJP (reverse-mode). Report the ratio."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 13. 🔵 Hessian-Vector Products\nShow that the Hessian-vector product $H \\mathbf{v}$ can be computed using one forward-mode pass on top of one reverse-mode pass. Implement this for $f(x, y) = x^2 y + y^3$."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 14. 🔴 Gradient of Batch Normalization\nDerive $\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial \\mathbf{x}_i}$, $\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial \\gamma}$, and $\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial \\beta}$ for batch normalization: $\\hat{x}_i = \\gamma \\frac{x_i - \\mu}{\\sqrt{\\sigma^2 + \\epsilon}} + \\beta$."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your derivation here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 15. 🔴 Vectorized Backprop for a Linear Layer\nDerive and implement $\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial W}$ and $\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial \\mathbf{x}}$ for a linear layer $\\mathbf{y} = W\\mathbf{x} + \\mathbf{b}$ given upstream gradient $\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial \\mathbf{y}}$. Verify against PyTorch autograd."]},
